Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Arrays and Hypermatrices", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"137250ac-1b2c-ae47-a378-1290a10ab1d1"],

Cell["\<\
WolframInstitute`Hypergraphs` \[LongDash] the objects of the hypermatrix layer\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"7a81e8a5-19bf-be4b-9979-20f4e2d93221"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook shows the two kinds of array and the hypermatrix built out of \
them, together with the design choices behind them. Everything below is live \
output from src/.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54de6a59-3883-294b-9052-bbf2bf35dfcf"],

Cell["\<\
It goes on to the special arrays, the contraction operation ArrayMultiply, \
the entry-by-entry operations that make arrays multilinear, and the search \
for equational identities between array operations. The graphical rendering \
of 1-, 2- and 3-arrays is the one part of this layer still to come.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"afe95ce3-9a32-e442-8bff-b7d45fbe3b15"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Loading the package", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ae089598-87eb-214c-ad7e-3d2ea554bdb2"],

Cell["\<\
Get[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"src\", \
\"Hypergraph.wl\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f09b2421-a48e-b94e-beed-87ba77f34133"],

Cell["\<\
The arrays and hypermatrices live in src/Hypermatrix.wl, which the core file \
pulls in, so one Get still brings in the whole package.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d50db189-15b1-c048-9616-d76905b3c29c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Numerical arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a795ad10-b399-324b-88db-ec9f58c67376"],

Cell["\<\
An array in the Wolfram Language is a nesting of lists. A numerical array \
wraps such a nesting together with the value domain its entries are drawn \
from.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8df39d2a-acde-bb4a-8f55-4bd8518a3541"],

