D->"b88ce9b6-55c0-0741-94dc-9c03ab8d3c91"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The two 1-arrays come first, shorter dimensions before longer. The three \
2-arrays follow, all of dimensions 2\[Times]2, separated by symmetry. The \
3-array comes last.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c164e5e-cf1c-5e4e-bcb8-3d7622c0775a"],

Cell["\<\
Because the order is canonical, the same arrays given differently produce the \
identical expression:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7058cc59-07f2-004e-899a-f36417df409e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Hypermatrix[{NumericalArray[{1, 2}], NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}]}] ===
 Hypermatrix[{NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}], NumericalArray[{1, 2}]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f34ec910-0973-e84c-923a-4e58bcf31d96"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"214a0276-9f0a-4344-8e5e-2d8d89d6a94f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Two arrays alike in order, dimensions and symmetry are put in the Wolfram \
Language's own canonical order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the \
set of arrays it was given and of nothing else. Without that last tiebreak \
the three 2\[Times]2 arrays above could come out in either of two orders \
depending on how they were typed."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"1db8dd7f-72dc-e64c-a531-1c56ce680f22"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["What goes in", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2774e222-0b70-b54c-abce-8fed697ad603"],

Cell["\<\
Raw entries are promoted to numerical arrays, and the two kinds of array may \
be mixed:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bfbf32c4-38a3-db45-8a9e-26b0bb50b13a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Hypermatrix[{{1, 2}, {1.5, 2.5}, SymbolicArray[a, {2, 2}]}][\"Domains\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8fb9e24e-9ff1-a941-9350-6709538f3125"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Symbolic\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"e18b4c87-edce-b242-ba73-f49e84d8d88c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, HypermatrixArrays gives them, and Normal \
gives their entries in the same order:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a3e55b2-77a5-f147-975c-fa71aa8f16f4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
hm2 = Hypermatrix[{{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}, {1, 2}}];
{Length[hm2], Normal[hm2]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"90e6b413-7df5-5343-a6d8-11d6edae0814"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"2", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",E\
xpressionUUID->"cc902b18-e85e-4241-8ad0-4effa8592d6f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["A sequence of arrays is accepted as well as a list:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e14074cd-7f4a-cc40-abf1-15d4fa338dfa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Hypermatrix[NumericalArray[{1, 2}], NumericalArray[{1, 2, 3}]] ===
 Hypermatrix[{NumericalArray[{1, 2}], NumericalArray[{1, 2, 3}]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"496d8b04-2981-e34d-a499-12741b12342d"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f43c8b2c-0440-8e48-8840-20b12fc01c4a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Anything that is not an array is refused:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a7c7dcc-4237-1849-ba5c-6f12186ec042"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Quiet @ Hypermatrix[{\"nope\"}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ff6af210-1e49-3247-a74e-2e062e53db95"],

Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"6de111f7-2850-d741-a17a-d68e5983a123"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Special arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5f9ae41a-fa72-0742-a65d-8d6645944dde"],

Cell["\<\
The constant arrays and the generalized Kronecker deltas are available in any \
order, dimension and value domain. Each declares the strongest symmetry that \
actually holds of it, which the NumericalArray constructor then verifies.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"640f27d8-298f-d447-9d2a-8575de254294"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["{Normal @ ZeroArray[2, 3], Normal @ OneArray[2, 3]}", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9e29a1d8-2e4b-2243-a22d-c40c0c8ef1d7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",Ex\
pressionUUID->"ca775507-9425-024d-a013-5e468e3c617b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The identity array is one where all of its indices agree. At order two it is \
the identity matrix; at order three it is one only on the main diagonal:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56868186-b290-7941-a27b-59aa39de2b77"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["{Normal @ IdentityArray[2, 3], Normal @ IdentityArray[3, 2]}", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f9671cc1-0014-d741-8d99-ccab72066271"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",E\
xpressionUUID->"41cead5b-0b3f-b144-8f93-50a70d326bb7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
A partial identity is one where the indices at chosen positions agree, \
whatever the others do. These are the three partial identities of a 3-array, \
one per pair of indices:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8c13f94c-9593-e548-862c-d34d0a7972da"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Normal @ PartialIdentityArray[3, 2, #] & /@ {{1, 2}, {2, 3}, {1, 3}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a2c7be6c-170e-a546-b9a5-112ea19ad1b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",E\
xpressionUUID->"97b407ec-3d85-cf49-929f-47896c8bd5d7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "A constant array and a full identity are invariant under every permutation \
of their indices, so they are declared symmetric. A partial identity on only \
some positions is not, so it is declared rigid. Naming every position gives \
back the full identity exactly."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"df870f26-eed5-c04f-86fe-60d2395c874e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
{ArraySymmetry @ ZeroArray[3, 2], ArraySymmetry @ IdentityArray[3, 2],
  ArraySymmetry @ PartialIdentityArray[3, 2, {1, 2}],
  PartialIdentityArray[3, 2, {1, 2, 3}] === IdentityArray[3, 2]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"708a7ecf-0562-3d43-82a4-b673ecc33bb4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Symmetric\"\>", ",", "\<\"Symmetric\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rigid\"\>",
    ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"18945adf-e91e-f749-b557-\
ddc4bbc9720c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Contraction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"36db8da7-5fb1-5b40-8874-317f42059eb8"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayMultiply contracts a list of arrays according to an index specification, \
in the manner of Einstein summation. Indices named in the output survive; the \
rest are summed over.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2bca8d8-0623-6e4e-aa87-596de6ae5a8f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
a = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}}; b = {{0, 1}, {1, 0}};
ArrayMultiply[{a, b}, \"ij,jk->ik\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2b297c3c-f256-a446-8b2e-8750f0c71ed3"],

